WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:02.336
Describe "Cha Cha Real Smooth" in three words.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.218
Describe "Cha Cha" in three words.

00:00:09.301 --> 00:00:09.718
Okay.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.261
It's so good.

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:18.936
I can't believe college is over.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.062
You have a job now, or...

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:22.397
We're not allowed to talk about jobs
at the Bat Mitzvah party.

00:00:22.481 --> 00:00:25.150
So, you either don't have a job,
or you have a bad job.

00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:27.277
I have a bad job, yeah.

00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:28.070
Ooh, okay.

00:00:28.153 --> 00:00:31.615
What is the secret to becoming
an exceptional party starter?

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:32.658
A savior complex.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:35.702
No.
The key is to come outside of yourself,

00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:37.162
but that's also the danger too.

00:00:37.246 --> 00:00:39.665
How much does a party starter
get paid, I wonder.

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:43.043
I think they said just under
what an unhappy pharmaceutical exec makes.

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:44.211
What the hell does that mean?

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:45.629
Do you believe in soulmates?

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.631
-I believe in soulmates, yes.
-Yeah, me too.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:51.468
I think on the earth,
we all have like a ton of soulmates.

00:00:51.552 --> 00:00:53.011
You annoy me more than anybody
in the whole world.

00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:54.972
-Right, but you also love me more than--
-But I love you so much.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.306
More than anyone in the world.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.308
Mmm... I love you so much.

00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:01.562
I'll bet you three hundred dollars
that I can get Lola on a dance floor.

00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:03.480
I will give you a thousand dollars.

00:01:04.648 --> 00:01:06.525
Margaret told me that she wants to kiss.

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:07.401
Uh-oh.

00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:09.444
Do you remember your first kiss?

00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:11.196
My first kiss was...
(makes kissing sound)

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.825
I was at night in a skate park
and, like, I wasn't supposed to be there.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.118
And it was, like, cool.

00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:18.120
-Naturally.
-I'm not lying.

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:20.789
What was it like having Leslie Mann
as your mom?

00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:22.791
I really thought of her as my mom,

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:25.252
so after each scene
I was expecting her to be like,

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:26.336
"Good job!"

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.463
It's so cute. It's so good.

00:01:28.547 --> 00:01:30.090
But I would forget that I'm--

00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:31.216
-The director?
-The director.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.801
You have a job to do right now.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:36.013
Why did you pick "Cha Cha Real Smooth"
as the title of the film?

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.974
It's the part in the dance
where you do your own dance.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.393
That's the best answer
you've given of

00:01:41.476 --> 00:01:43.103
any question I've ever heard
you've been asked.

00:01:43.437 --> 00:01:44.563
Thank you so much.

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:46.607
Have you ever been to Funkytown?

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:49.276
If not,
would you like to go to Funkytown?

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:50.277
Of course.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.695
I think we killed it.

